        ['If audio is interrupted', 'Reconnect your headphones, confirm they are selected as the output, and try again. An active scene can continue in the background until you stop it. When Live Activities are enabled, iOS can show the scene and elapsed time on the Dynamic Island and Lock Screen. Playback stops immediately if the audio route is lost or another audio session interrupts it.'],
        ['What SCENE does with sound', 'Nearby sound is processed live in memory on your iPhone. It is never recorded, saved, transcribed, uploaded, or retained. SCENE has no account, ads, trackers, analytics SDKs, cloud service, or AI.'],
        ['Contact support', 'Email eastnoise26@gmail.com with the app version, iOS version, headphone model, and the state shown in the app. Do not send recordings or sensitive content.'],
      ],
    },
    privacy: {
      kicker: 'SCENE · PRIVACY',
      title: 'Your sound stays with you.',
      lead: 'This policy explains what happens to microphone audio and other data when you use SCENE.',
      updated: 'Effective August 26, 2026',
      sections: [
        ['Microphone audio', 'SCENE uses the microphone only after you tap Start, grant permission, and connect supported headphones. Audio is processed live in device memory to apply effects and drive the reactive visual. It is never recorded, saved, transcribed, uploaded, or retained. An active scene can continue in the background until you stop it and ends immediately if the audio route is lost, another audio session interrupts it, or the audio engine fails.'],
